       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1,700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is about twice the maximum. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- Something else\n\nIf you really want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a rationale. I can add it to the order note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
